@title 3D Heat: Cabinet shell block after a run shows the heat split and face temperatures as model
@area 3D
@sizes 1366x768 1920x1080
# Lane H7. After a Quick run the Heat panel has a "Cabinet shell" fold: how the heat leaves (convection, radiation, other) as a bar with watts, and the temperature of each face inside and outside, labelled model.
open_starter_example
wait 20
click_text 3D #1
wait 30
click_text Heat #1
wait 20
click_text Cancel
wait 10
click_text Auto #1
wait 10
try click_text Cancel
wait 30
click_text "Settings for the next run"
wait 10
click_text Quick
wait 10
click_text Simulate #2
wait_s 120
scroll 1150 600 -400
wait 20
click_text "Cabinet shell"
wait 20
scroll 1150 600 -600
wait 20
expect "Through the shell"
expect "model"
shot shell-result
check_layout
check_blank shell-result
